### Assessment of Missing at Random Assumption

To assess whether missingness in 90-day outcomes was associated with key baseline covariates, we generated shadow plots comparing the distribution of each covariate among patients with observed versus missing values. If the distributions are similar, this supports the MAR assumption — that missingness is conditionally independent of the unobserved outcome given the observed covariates.

